texto_original:
Netflix documentary about Brazilian woman that murdered and dismembered his Japanese husband. Doing my research about the Asian American experience dating in South America I stumbled across a Netflix documentary called  "Elize Matsunaga: Once Upon a Crime" which consists of 4 episodes. 

I highly recommend if you are Asian to binge it to try to understand how Asians are perceived in South America. From what I've been able to digest is that South Americans tend to see Asians as privileged with a secure income.

The victim was Marcos Kitano Matsunaga was the heir of the food company "Yoki". Marcos met her future wife a White Brazilian **Elize Araújo Giacomini in an escort website.**

**He ended up marrying her and having a daughter but was unable to satisfy his womanizing ways and kept hooking up with escorts to the point that he even made reviews about his experiences in forums dedicated to the escort experience.**

The rest you can make the conjectures. 

With recent cases of the dangers of dating in Colombia. I've been also considering Brazil and Peru from reading that Asians are numerous in those countries and I won't stand out as much as in Colombia. The thing is I wonder how genuine dating is in those countries in a way I could read their intentions if they are truly interested in me or my money. I have no connections nor friends to go with.

